me>Berstad</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intestinal gas in plain abdominal radiographs does not correlate with symptoms after lactulose challenge</article-title><source>Eur J Gastroenterol</source><year>2007</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>589</fpage><lpage>593</lpage></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="f1-bmi-2009-009" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Abdominal plain radiograph of case 1 on admission showed a markedly dilated small bowel, with no dilatation of the colon.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2009-009f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-bmi-2009-009" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>An abdominal computerized tomography (CT) showed largely distended small bowel loops and a smooth transition zone (arrow) at the site of obstruction.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2009-009f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-bmi-2009-009" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Clinical course of case 1. Changes in breath hydrogen concentration and abdominal plain radiographs on representative dates are demonstrated.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2009-009f3"/></fig><fig id="f4-bmi-2009-009" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Abdominal plain radiograph of case 2 on admission showed multiple dilated gas-filled small-bowel loops, with no dilatation of the colon one day after undergoing surgical treatment.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2009-009f4"/></fig><fig id="f5-bmi-2009-009" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Clinical course of case 2 after a treatment with erythromycin. Changes in breath hydrogen concentration and abdominal plain radiographs on representative dates are demonstrated.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2009-009f5"/></fig></floats-group></article>